Hey! Thanks for the good tool :)

I'd like to use a custom set of default materials instead of the default ones, and I thought it would be more convenient to do that through an input file instead of applying a patch every time master is updated.

I have implemented a way to read json files with material defaults. Consider a file `material-defaults.json`, for example with the following data:

```javascript
{
  "IfcWall": {
    "diffuse": [0.964, 0.913, 0.729]
  },
  "IfcSlab": {
    "diffuse": [0.8, 1, 1]
  },
  "IfcSpace": {
    "diffuse": [0.6, 0.8, 0],
    "transparency": 0.8
  }
}
```

Then, though a new CLI flag, you can refer to that file by using the new option `--default-material-file material-defaults.json`. Except for the toplevel default value, all the default values will be replaced by this.

I don't think this is ready to be merged down yet though, as I have not yet added documentation, and I'm pretty sure you'd like to have better error handling (as of now, there isn't any at all). I'd need some help with the error handling, as this is literally my first lines of C++ and I'm not sure how to do that idiomatically.

I'm also curious if you think using normalised RGB values is better than hexadecimal RGB values or not. I just implemented normalised RGB ones as that was the easiest, but that could be changed.

