I tracked the issue in line 641 of import_ifc.py. It seems that the script assumes that the element is a IfcGeometricRepresentationSubContext, when it is in fact a IfcGeometricRepresentationContext that has no TargetView attribute. I tried modifying the following code snippet:

    def add_product_representation_contexts(self, element, obj):
        subcontexts = []
        if element.is_a('IfcProduct'):
            if not element.Representation:
                return
            for r in element.Representation.Representations:
                subcontexts.append('{}/{}/{}'.format(
                    r.ContextOfItems.ContextType,
                    r.ContextOfItems.ContextIdentifier,
                    r.ContextOfItems.TargetView))
    ...

into:

    def add_product_representation_contexts(self, element, obj):
        subcontexts = []
        if element.is_a('IfcProduct'):
            if not element.Representation:
                return
            for r in element.Representation.Representations:
                if r.ContextOfItems.is_a('IfcGeometricRepresentationContext'):
                    for s in r.ContextOfItems.HasSubContexts:				
                        subcontexts.append('{}/{}/{}'.format(
                            s.ContextType,
                            s.ContextIdentifier,
                            s.TargetView))
                else:
                        subcontexts.append('{}/{}/{}'.format(
                            r.ContextOfItems.ContextType,
                            r.ContextOfItems.ContextIdentifier,
                            r.ContextOfItems.TargetView))
    ...

